WEBVTT

00:00:02.314 --> 00:00:03.564
What are you doing?

00:00:03.564 --> 00:00:05.733
Do you know how much I've put into this?

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:08.611
How much you have put into this? I guess...

00:00:08.611 --> 00:00:10.322
Don't look in his beautiful eyes.

00:00:10.322 --> 00:00:11.948
[PETER & BEA SIGH]

00:00:11.948 --> 00:00:14.617
I need to go and get my family, Nigel. Goodbye.

00:00:14.617 --> 00:00:16.953
Your books will never go anywhere without me.

00:00:16.953 --> 00:00:20.748
This is the last the world will ever hear about Peter Rabbit.

00:00:20.748 --> 00:00:22.542
I'll take my chances.

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:24.336
Come on, Peter.

00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:28.965
Goodbye, Nigel.

00:00:28.965 --> 00:00:30.300
[INHALES SHARPLY]

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.261
Oh, we're making a terrible mistake.

00:00:33.261 --> 00:00:34.846
What can we do to make--? Thomas!

00:00:34.846 --> 00:00:37.682
[♪♪♪]

00:00:40.268 --> 00:00:42.603
Okay, where are we on Winnie the Pooh?

00:00:42.603 --> 00:00:44.689
BEA: Okay, where's the first stop?

00:00:44.689 --> 00:00:46.483
PETER: 440 Riverside Drive.

00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:47.859
BEA: Did you just talk?

00:00:47.859 --> 00:00:49.652
THOMAS: Let's say it was just the radio.

00:00:49.652 --> 00:00:52.947
PETER: This is BBC 7 playing all the hits with none of the...

00:00:52.947 --> 00:00:56.576
NARRATOR: So away they went to retrieve the rest of their family.

00:00:56.576 --> 00:00:59.079
There we are. The first was easy.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:01.081
Okay, number two. THOMAS: Here we go.

00:01:02.332 --> 00:01:05.752
The next was a little pricklier.

00:01:08.046 --> 00:01:09.005
[QUIET KNOCK]

00:01:09.005 --> 00:01:10.507
[SCREAMING]

00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:14.428
But the rest were much trickier.

00:01:14.428 --> 00:01:15.929
[WHIMPERING]

00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:18.181
Hello. There's been some misunderstanding

00:01:18.181 --> 00:01:20.183
in regards to the custody of that rabbit.

00:01:20.183 --> 00:01:23.853
I promised the missus stew. Ah!

00:01:23.853 --> 00:01:26.398
So they set off on a rescue mission,

00:01:26.398 --> 00:01:30.193
the likes of which Bea insisted never happened in her world.

00:01:30.193 --> 00:01:32.195
[♪♪♪]

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.871
Benjamin, I'm really sorry. Listen, I never should have--

00:01:41.871 --> 00:01:44.207
Not now, Peter. Get me out of here!

00:01:44.207 --> 00:01:45.666
Yep.

00:01:50.464 --> 00:01:52.006
[ENGINE REVVING] [LAUGHING]

00:01:57.512 --> 00:02:00.474
They're the rabbits from that book.

00:02:00.474 --> 00:02:02.601
Benjamin, I'm really sorry. Listen--

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:05.145
Not now either. Right. Right.

00:02:05.145 --> 00:02:07.355
[♪♪♪]

00:02:08.565 --> 00:02:10.233
[YELLING]

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.528
[STUDENTS CHATTERING]

00:02:15.155 --> 00:02:16.948
[STUDENTS GASPING, LAUGHING]

00:02:24.205 --> 00:02:26.207
No! Oh!

00:02:26.207 --> 00:02:28.042
We're too late! We're too--

00:02:28.042 --> 00:02:29.919
Felix is gone! Get up.

00:02:29.919 --> 00:02:32.964
Oh. Come on, let's go. Quick. Quick.

00:02:32.964 --> 00:02:35.175
Let's go. Let's go. Hey.

00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:37.385
[♪♪♪]

00:02:40.847 --> 00:02:43.975
[SPEAKS IN GERMAN] [TOMMY WHIMPERING]

00:02:48.813 --> 00:02:50.607
[TOMMY YELLS, LAUGHING]

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.782
[ALL YELLING]

00:03:03.077 --> 00:03:04.745
[ALL SHUDDERING]

00:03:12.504 --> 00:03:13.630
[JEMIMA SCREAMS]

00:03:19.093 --> 00:03:20.554
Huh?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.558
[SIGHS]

00:03:24.558 --> 00:03:25.850
[TIRES SCREECHING]

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.311
Brake lights.

00:03:33.316 --> 00:03:35.860
[SHOP BELL JINGLES] [CUSTOMERS CHATTERING]

00:03:38.488 --> 00:03:40.740
[GRUNTS, YELLS] [SHIVERING]

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.075
Oh, thank goodness.

00:03:42.075 --> 00:03:43.743
Could you come back in 25 minutes?

00:03:43.743 --> 00:03:46.037
This is doing wonders for my skin.

00:03:46.037 --> 00:03:48.248
BUTCHER: Hey!

00:03:48.248 --> 00:03:49.790
Hey, that's my pig!

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.918
[TIRES SQUEALING]

00:03:51.918 --> 00:03:54.254
[ENGINE REVVING] [TIRES SQUEALING]

00:03:54.254 --> 00:03:56.089
[♪♪♪]

00:03:58.258 --> 00:03:59.342
[ALL GASPING]

00:04:01.219 --> 00:04:02.470
Whoa!

00:04:08.435 --> 00:04:11.771
[PEDESTRIANS YELLING] [TIGGY-WINKLE GRUNTING]

00:04:11.771 --> 00:04:14.274
[LAUGHING]

00:04:17.068 --> 00:04:19.487
[ELECTRICAL CRACKLING] [SHUDDERING]

00:04:20.905 --> 00:04:23.032
[GROANING] [TIRE SQUEALS]

00:04:27.161 --> 00:04:30.331
And that's why I'm on the billboard.

00:04:31.916 --> 00:04:33.627
[ALL SCREAMING]

00:04:38.632 --> 00:04:41.342
"Lavatory"? That's what it means?

00:04:41.342 --> 00:04:43.344
The place where men read the newspaper?

00:04:43.344 --> 00:04:45.597
Yeah. You don't have to change your name.

00:04:45.597 --> 00:04:47.014
There's no one in the world

00:04:47.014 --> 00:04:49.392
I'd rather be confused with than you, Flops.

00:04:49.392 --> 00:04:51.686
Same here, Mops. Mm.

00:04:54.648 --> 00:04:56.816
NARRATOR: With everyone safely reunited,

00:04:56.816 --> 00:05:00.612
they headed back to Gloucester for one final rescue,

00:05:00.612 --> 00:05:04.198
which Peter knew to be the most dangerous of all.

00:05:04.198 --> 00:05:06.409
[♪♪♪]

00:05:11.998 --> 00:05:13.333
[GRUNTS]

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:16.043
BARNABAS: I underestimated you, son.

00:05:16.043 --> 00:05:18.755
[GASPS] [RABBITS WHIMPERING]

00:05:18.755 --> 00:05:22.091
This whole time, I thought I was the one playing you.

00:05:22.091 --> 00:05:25.136
Looks like I was the one being played.

00:05:28.431 --> 00:05:30.183
Where's the rest of it?

00:05:32.435 --> 00:05:36.230
Same place this is going. With us.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.107
You know who you're dealing with?

00:05:38.107 --> 00:05:41.611
Yeah. The guy who got me to put my family in danger.

00:05:41.611 --> 00:05:43.946
But that's not your fault. It's mine.

00:05:43.946 --> 00:05:45.865
I convinced them.

00:05:45.865 --> 00:05:48.159
I believed this is who I was.

00:05:48.159 --> 00:05:49.369
Now I know better.

00:05:49.369 --> 00:05:51.120
You don't know nothing, kid.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.790
Oh, no. You did teach me a couple of things.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.291
Oh, yeah? Like what?

00:05:55.291 --> 00:05:56.501
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.419
Once a week, the old tailor upstairs

00:05:58.419 --> 00:06:00.505
drives to the market to buy his sausage.

00:06:00.505 --> 00:06:02.923
It's a real love story. What of it?

00:06:02.923 --> 00:06:04.676
And the second thing is:

00:06:04.676 --> 00:06:06.845
The rabbit comes out of the hole,

00:06:06.845 --> 00:06:08.555
goes around the tree

00:06:08.555 --> 00:06:10.682
and back down the hole.

00:06:10.682 --> 00:06:11.932
What?

00:06:11.932 --> 00:06:13.309
[YELLING]

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.439
[GASPS, YELLING]

00:06:18.439 --> 00:06:21.067
[GASPS, GROANING]

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:23.152
Huh? Huh?

00:06:23.152 --> 00:06:24.904
Ugh... Huh?

00:06:24.904 --> 00:06:26.155
[CLICKS TONGUE]

00:06:26.155 --> 00:06:28.991
[YELLS, GROANING]

00:06:31.118 --> 00:06:32.662
[ALL PANTING]

